From ac3c4377576ef907fc44294e03067699f9290b52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:34:39 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(api): backfill finished-match lineups and timeline on
 demand
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sync's "recent finishers" rule only re-summarizes a finished
match if 1h < hoursSinceSync < 26h, so a match that finished while
the server was down (or more than 26h ago) sat with zero
match_player_stats and zero timeline_events forever. The lineups
and timeline tabs both read "not out yet" for matches that were
already played.

Fix: in the /api/matches/:id/lineups and /api/matches/:id/timeline
route handlers, when the DB has zero rows for a finished match,
call syncMatchSummary(league, matchId) once and re-query. The
summary writes to match_player_stats and timeline_events, so the
first user to open the match pays one ESPN fetch and every
subsequent user gets the cached result.

Failure mode is graceful: if the ESPN fetch throws, the route
falls through to the empty state rather than 500'ing.

