From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:47:09 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(lineups): goal, assist, card badges and subs row on
 the pitch
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Lineups tab showed the starting XI and the bench, but a
finished match had no per-player signal for what they actually
did — a scorer looked the same as a non-scorer, a sub who came
on and scored wasn't on the pitch at all.

Fix: LineupsTab now also reads the timeline events and passes a
per-player event map (goals, assists, subIn/subOut minute, card
type) down to LineupsPanel. Starters who scored show a ball per
goal, assisters an "A", carded players the same yellow/red
rectangle the timeline draws. A new "Subs used" row below the
pitch lists players who came off the bench with their minute, the
same badges, and an ↑ arrow.

Upcoming matches with no events render exactly as before — the
new map is empty, no badges, no subs row.

